  "operation": "conditional-climb-trace-development",
  "why_this_direction": "A shared update can repair multiple operations only if the fitted loss represents each failure. The present downhill field omitted the climb error. Compare archived routes with the same downhill error and requested climb height, then evaluate a same-question checkpoint that repaired climb alone.",
  "repeating_pattern_check": "Outcome-correlated turn fields can read back a downstream arithmetic decision. Leave complete source families out when selecting a cell and test a documented same-prompt climb-only improvement separately.",
  "what_went_wrong_before": "A global downhill score and an inherited fitted loss logged outside the gradient cannot train climb. Earlier transfer checks confused a physical repair with the right final verdict.",
  "hypothesis": "At matched downhill behavior there is recurring separately measurable information in the computational trace about double counting the climb height.",
  "prediction": "A field chosen entirely from the donor families separates a development failed climb from valid climbs and decreases on the same-question checkpoint that repairs climb while retaining the downhill error.",
  "would_weaken_it": "No supported field, no common cells, errors ranking on the wrong side, or no decrease on the documented climb-only intervention weakens this candidate. Endpoint association cannot alone locate a cause.",
  "rule": "Use the full native direction field at every decoded prediction with the existing prefix registrar. All eligible witnesses have a 1 m requested climb and incorrectly subtract downhill work. Freeze signed donor contrasts that classify each left-out family, then score the discovery-00 and discovery-01 families and checkpoint 175 without refitting. Both family and height selection are specific to this development comparison. The result is retrospective. Timing and correct answers never select match positions.",
